  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 94a9804fffdeb7549880071e0e3bcbee, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  centerMessageText: {fileID: 211845430}
  totalPointsBar: {fileID: 793156282}
  barFill: {fileID: 1829659758}
  percentageText: {fileID: 203624486}
  rankText: {fileID: 2027067790}
  suggestionText: {fileID: 1488264194}
  maxTotalPoints: 60
  animationDuration: 2
  typewriterSpeed: 0.05
  mainMenuBuildIndex: 0
  overallRanks:
  - Maladaptive Perfectionism and Emotional Burnout
  - Learned Helplessness and Perfectionistic Depression
  - Avoidant Procrastination and Conditional Self-Worth
  - Adaptive Perfectionism
  - Self-Compassion
  suggestionRank0: The score possible maladaptive perfectionism combined with emotional
    burnout, and you may have anxiety-depression comorbidity. You can try to do a
    small action daily, like a 10-minute walk without checking your phone. It can
    rebuild a sense of control
  suggestionRank1: You may have learned helplessness or perfectionistic depression.
    You can try the 3-minute Self-Compassion Break daily or 5 to 15 minutes of mindful
    breathing. It can help shift from inner pressure to inner safety.
  suggestionRank2: "You may be showing avoidant procrastination and conditional self-worth.
    First, you can set 1\u20132 \u201Cgood enough\u201D micro-goals each day and
    note the positive feelings afterward. Reading about self-compassion or practicing.
    Moreover, talking to a trusted friend or counselor will speed up the change.
    \r\n"
  suggestionRank3: You are close to adaptive perfectionism which can become more
    friendly and support myself. You can try 5 minutes of mindful breathing. It will
    bring you closer to optimal mental health.
  suggestionRank4: You already practice high levels of self-compassion. You can treating
    yourself. Please kindness rather than harsh self-criticism. You can keep up small
    daily habits like gratitude journaling
  openingMessage: "Journey complete, Alice. \nYour total score: {0}/135. \nThis is
    your report. Let's look at your mental state and give some gentle opinion."
  thankYouMessage: "Your kingdom will grow and heal as you do. \nNo matter your score,
    you have bravely completed this journey. \n\nGoodbye, Alice."
